  "tutorialDone": "Let us start!",
  "tutorial1Title": "Welcome to Carcassonne Counter!",
  "tutorial1Body": "A score counter for Carcassonne that supports expansions. A few steps will show you how to use it.",
  "tutorial2Title": "Add players",
  "tutorial2Body": "Use the \"+\" button to add players (at least two are needed) and pick their meeple colors. Press and hold a player row to edit or delete it.",
  "tutorialExpansionsTitle": "Choose expansions",
  "tutorialExpansionsBody": "Before the game starts, turn on the expansions you play with: pick \"Expansions\" in the menu or use the \"Modify expansions\" button in the start dialog. The \"All expansions\" switch turns them all on at once.",
  "tutorial3Title": "Start the game",
  "tutorial3Body": "When everything is ready, press \"Start game\". From then on you cannot change players or expansions.",
  "tutorial4Title": "Add points",
  "tutorial4Body": "Tap a player row, choose what you are scoring (city, road, cloister, farm or an expansion element), enter the result and confirm.",
  "tutorial5Title": "A mistake?",
  "tutorial5Body": "In the menu you can undo the most recently confirmed points. The \"Rules summary\" lists the scoring of each element, and the \"?\" icon next to options shows an explanation.",
  "tutorial6Title": "End of the game",
  "tutorial6Body": "The flag button ends the game and shows the winner. The \"Summary\" button opens a table of the points from each source, and \"New game\" lets you start again.\n\nHave fun!",
  "aboutTitle": "About the app",
  "aboutVersion": "Version {version}",
  "aboutDescription": "A score counter for the Carcassonne board game. It scores by the rules, supports many expansions, guides the game flow and shows a summary at the end.",
  "aboutMadeBy": "Made by {author}",
  "aboutDisclaimer": "An unofficial fan-made app. Carcassonne is a trademark of its owners. All icons in the app are original.",
  "aboutLicenses": "Library licenses",
  "newGameChoiceBody": "Do you want to play again with the same players, or set the players up from scratch?\n\nPoints, goods and used circus tokens will be reset. Expansions stay as they are, and you can still change them before starting.",
