  "rulesGermanCastles": "• Each player receives 1 castle (2 with 2–3 players). A castle is placed instead of drawing a tile and may not touch other castles, even diagonally.\n• Castle lord: a completed castle (surrounded like a cloister) scores 12 pts. An unfinished one at the end of the game scores 2 pts for the castle tile and 1 pt for each surrounding tile.\n• A completed road or city with a castle at its end scores the majority players 3 pts per castle, even an unoccupied one. The bonus is added after the inn and cathedral modifiers.\n• Castles give no +3 bonus for unfinished features (at the end of the game).\n• A castle does not count as a city when farms or a barn are scored: it brings no points to farmers or to the barn owner.",
  "rulesGermanCathedrals": "• The expansion contains 6 tiles with cathedrals in the fields, with 3 or 4 roads leading from the cathedral.\n• Highwayman on a road to a cathedral: double points per segment, that is 2 pts per tile (3 with an inn). This also applies to a road unfinished at the end of the game (0 with an inn).\n• The archbishop on the cathedral scores only when all the roads leading from the cathedral are closed: 1 pt per road segment (2 with an inn), each segment on the cathedral tile counted separately. If any road stays open until the end of the game, the archbishop scores nothing.",
